    "created_at": "2020-02-11T16:48:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-11T16:48:14Z",
    "body": "> If the list changes such that it contains a single node, would you then no longer return the list? \r\n\r\nThat's a good question.  In Gecko, it looks like yes: when the list becomes length-1 we forget the list and just point to the one element; if the length then becomes longer than 1 we create a new list.  I don't know what other browsers do.\r\n",
